      "title": "Running a City Marathon",
      "text": "Taking part in a city marathon is a challenge that requires months of preparation. Many runners start training at least six months before the big day. It is important to (1) ______ a training plan that gradually increases the distance you run each week. This helps your body get used to the physical stress and prevents injuries. On the day of the race, the atmosphere is usually incredible. Thousands of people line the streets to cheer for the runners, which provides a huge boost of (2) ______ when you feel tired. It is essential to stay hydrated throughout the race, so make sure you (3) ______ advantage of the water stations along the route. Many participants find that the most difficult part is the final five kilometers. However, seeing the finish line gives you the (4) ______ to keep going. Crossing that line is a moment of pure joy and a great (5) ______ of achievement. Whether you finish in three hours or six, completing a marathon is something you will always be (6) ______ of.",
      "passageVocab": [
        "preparation",
        "atmosphere",
        "hydrated",
        "achievement",
        "proud"
      ]
